1 NOTE @NI118@
0 @NI118@ NOTE
1 CONC It is believed that Ann was of the group of families (Henzey, Tizick and 
1 CONC Tittery) that brought glassmaking to England from France. The name Tizick 
1 CONC ssems to have been corrupted over time of the original version of the 
1 CONC 1500's: 
1 CONT
1 CONT      de Thisac -> Tyzack -> Tizick.
1 CONT
1 CONT After searches in the main population areas of France, only one person of 
1 CONC the name de Thisac has been found:
1 CONT
1 CONT      Janine Ardenne do Tizac, 365 r
1 CONT      Vaugirard, 75015, Paris. (1) 45 32 30 70.
1 CONT
1 CONT There appears to be a few people scattered around Cornwall, Wiltshire and 
1 CONC one in Dover, Kent with this surname (Tizick/Tyzack).
